[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done — [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m now reads [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 120[39m. That's the only change.

  I tried to run [38;5;153mserver.js[39m to confirm the value prints, and it failed — but not because of this edit. An ancestor
  [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m in the enclosing evals tree sets [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m, so Node treats [38;5;153mserver.js[39m's [38;5;153mrequire()[39m as invalid ESM.
  That's a pre-existing artifact of where this directory sits, present before my change; I left it alone as out of
  scope. So the value is verified by inspection, not by execution.

  Standing security note, now that it's 2h rather than 8h: idle expiry is still the only bound on a stolen token's
  lifetime here — there's no revocation or logout path in these two files. Worth having one eventually, but that's a
  separate piece of work.

